You are a senior product designer and full-stack engineer. Build a complete, polished, production-quality web app called **ShareShelf**, a neighborhood item-sharing platform, for a social-good hackathon. It must be fully working end to end, with real data in Supabase. Write complete code for every screen and flow. No placeholders, no TODOs.

## 1. PRODUCT
Tagline: **Borrow what you need. Share what you have.**
People borrow everyday items (tools, books, electronics, camping gear, event supplies) from neighbors instead of buying things they only need briefly. Core journey: **Discover > Request > Approve > Borrow > Return > Complete.** The brand idea is **the loop**: things go out into the community and come back.

## 2. STACK
- React + TypeScript (use `any` where typing gets in the way so everything compiles), Tailwind CSS, `lucide-react`, `react-router-dom` (HashRouter), **`framer-motion`** for animation, `@supabase/supabase-js`.
- All data comes from Supabase. No hard-coded mock data in the UI.
- Read `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (also try `process.env` equivalents). If missing, show a friendly one-time "Connect Supabase" screen (Project URL + anon key fields), save in localStorage, and continue. Never crash on missing config.
- Files: `lib/supabase.ts`, `lib/api.ts` (all queries), `hooks/`, `components/`, `pages/`, `index.css`.

