## 7. SCREENS

### Discover (`/`)
- **Hero** (use the `Hero` component below): headline "Good things are better when shared.", supporting text "Borrow everyday essentials from your community, save money, and give useful things a second life.", buttons **Explore items** (navy) and **Share an item** (orange), a white pill "Your neighborhood is full of things worth sharing.", and on the right four real items from Supabase as floating cards on the ribbons. Do NOT invent user counts or statistics.
- A dismissible **"How the loop works"** strip with three animated steps: 1 Request, 2 Get approved, 3 Return. Tiny copy: "New here? Browse, request, return. That's the whole loop."
- **Search** (large rounded input, icon, clear button, live filtering by name, description, category, neighborhood), **category chips** with a sliding blue active pill, a neighborhood dropdown and an "Available now" toggle, plus a result count.
- **Item grid** (1/2/3/4 columns) of `ItemCard`s with staggered reveal on scroll. Loading: `SkeletonCard`s. Empty: "Nothing matches yet" with buttons "Clear filters" and "Ask your neighbors".

### Item details (sheet on mobile, centered modal on desktop)
Large image, name, category, condition, description, owner card, borrowing rules, FREE label, a **reserved dates** strip from `item_busy_dates`, and a short "How borrowing works" explainer. **Request to borrow** reveals the form inside the same sheet: start date, return date (min = today), optional message with a 300-character counter. Validate: not in the past, return not before start, no overlap with reserved ranges (inline: "Those dates overlap a reserved loan. Try another range."). On submit insert into `borrow_requests` (`status='pending'`, `owner_id` from the item), toast, then go to Activity > My requests. Owner viewing their own item sees "This is your item" with Edit and Remove.

### My activity (`/activity`)
Requires sign-in. Greeting "Hi, {first name}" with a one-line summary ("2 things need your attention"). Scrollable tabs with counts and a sliding underline: **My items, Incoming requests, Items I'm borrowing, My requests, Active loans, Completed exchanges**. Open on the tab with the most urgent action.
Each request is a card with the item thumbnail and name, the other person, dates, message, an animated **Stepper** (Requested > Approved > Picked up > Returned > Complete), a status badge, and role-based actions:
- Owner, `pending`: **Approve** (blue) and **Decline** (danger outline).
- Borrower, `pending` or `approved`: **Cancel request**.
- Borrower, `approved`: **I picked it up** (status `active`).
- Borrower, `active`: **Request return confirmation** (status `return_requested`).
- Owner, `return_requested`: **Confirm item returned** (status `completed`) and trigger `LoopBurst`.
Actions update Supabase with optimistic UI and rollback on error. **My items** tab: item list with availability toggle, Edit, Remove (confirmation sheet; block removal while a loan is approved or active, explaining why) and an **Add item** button. Every tab has a friendly empty state.

### Share an item (sheet on mobile, modal on desktop; also used for Edit)
Fields: name, description, category, condition, **photo upload** to `item-images` (drag and drop on desktop, camera/gallery on mobile, preview and remove) with an optional image URL alternative, neighborhood, availability, borrowing instructions, estimated replacement value in USD ("Used to estimate how much the community saves"). Inline validation. On save: toast, and the item appears in Discover immediately with a gentle entrance animation.

### Wanted board (`/wanted`)
Headline "Can't find it? Ask your neighbors." **Request an item** opens a form (item needed, description, category, neighborhood, date needed). Cards show title, description, category, neighborhood, "Needed by" date, requester, response count, **Respond** button. Respond opens a sheet listing responses plus a message box. The requester can mark it **fulfilled** or delete it. Category filter chips. Empty state invites the first request.

### Impact (`/impact`)
Read from the `community_impact` view only. Header with ribbons. Five big number cards using `CountUp` (animates when scrolled into view): **Items listed, Completed exchanges, Borrowed right now, Estimated money saved ($), Items reused**. Add a simple animated bar chart of items by category (computed from `items`, bars grow on view). A "How we calculate this" card: money saved is the sum of the estimated replacement value of items in completed exchanges; items reused counts distinct items borrowed and returned. Clear note: "Includes {demo_items} demonstration items. Figures are estimates, not real-world results." Never present fabricated statistics.

### Notifications
Bell dropdown (desktop, animated) and full-screen list (mobile) from the `notifications` table with relative times, unread highlight and "Mark all as read". Realtime arrivals also appear as toasts.

